DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20261228T063000
DTEND:20261228T072500
SUMMARY:[RW] Swim: technique and aerobic (55 min)
DESCRIPTION:8 min easy swim + kick\; 10 min drills (catch-up\, fingertip d
 rag\, sculling)\; 30 min steady aerobic\, RPE 3\; 5 min cool-down. Swim t
 ime and effort\, not distance: pools and paces differ. If you know your 1
 00 m time\, convert the minutes to metres. Rest 15-30 s between repeats.\
 n\nWeek 6 (BASE). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you move mea
 ns stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-12-29-run1-easy-run-with-stride@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20261229T063000
DTEND:20261229T080000
SUMMARY:[RW] Easy run with strides (90 min)
DESCRIPTION:10 min warm-up\; 67 min easy\; 6 x (0.33 min hard + 1 min easy
 )\; 5 min cool-down. Six relaxed fast strides of about 20 s (RPE 7\, smoo
 th\, not a sprint) with easy jogging between. Easy means RPE 2-3: you can
  talk in full sentences. Use your watch's easy heart-rate zone if you hav
 e one.\n\nWeek 6 (BASE). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you m
 ove means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
