DTSTART:20270130T063000
DTEND:20270130T102000
SUMMARY:[RW] Long ride (230 min)
DESCRIPTION:10 min warm-up\; 102 min easy\; 3 x (28 min steady + 8 min eas
 y)\; 10 min cool-down. Mostly steady endurance (RPE 2-3\, 56-75 % of FTP 
 if you use power). Eat and drink on rides over 90 minutes. Race-effort bl
 ocks (RPE 4-5): practise your race nutrition on these.\n\nWeek 10 (BUILD)
 . Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you move means stop.\nrampwi
 se-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-01-30-brick_run-brick-run-straight-o@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20270130T090000
DTEND:20270130T091500
SUMMARY:[RW] Brick run (straight off the bike) (15 min)
DESCRIPTION:15 min easy-steady run\, RPE 3-5. Legs often feel heavy for th
 e first 5 minutes: normal. Keep it easy: running straight after cycling c
 osts more energy than running fresh (Millet and Vleck 2000)\, and whether
  bricks improve that is unproven (Walsh 2019). Stop if anything hurts.\n\
 nWeek 10 (BUILD). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you move mea
 ns stop.\nrampwise-plan
